*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary

# Windows batch must reach the disk with CRLF. An LF-only .cmd made batch label
# resolution fail intermittently once already -- `rm` broke while `models`
# worked. Today this happens to work because Windows clones default to
# core.autocrlf=true; this states it so it does not depend on the cloner's
# configuration.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Python must reach the disk with LF on every platform. Without this the
# checked-out bytes depend on the cloner core.autocrlf, and 0.3.0a10 was built
# from a tree mixing CRLF and LF as a result -- byte-for-byte the same program,
# and an installed-content digest naming a tree no checkout can reproduce.
# Identity is asserted on installed content, so the content must not depend on
# who cloned it. Same reasoning as the *.cmd rule above, opposite ending.
*.py text eol=lf
